From 4a56eaf1c13503559755aca37010929692e8e049 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 11:39:55 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] NetInflow: workgroup size from the kernel launch; size(grid)
 in the kernels; p = 0 in the docstring (review)

- The pin kernels read their workgroup size with @uniform prod(@groupsize()) (static, since they are launched with
  StaticSize((256,))), replacing the deleted global constant.
- size(grid, 1) / size(grid, 2) instead of grid.Nx / grid.Ny in the kernels and configure_face_pins, as in face_length.
- NetInflow docstring: depth_exponent = 0 is the default.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Abhhvmt8meskhHGBgsw6yN
---
 .../open_boundary_utils.jl                    |  6 +-
 .../SplitExplicitFreeSurfaces.jl              |  2 +-
 .../barotropic_targeted_transport.jl          | 58 ++++++++++---------
 3 files changed, 34 insertions(+), 32 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/BoundaryConditions/open_boundary_schemes/open_boundary_utils.jl b/src/BoundaryConditions/open_boundary_schemes/open_boundary_utils.jl
index 6c0a651..01a804a 100644
--- a/src/BoundaryConditions/open_boundary_schemes/open_boundary_utils.jl
+++ b/src/BoundaryConditions/open_boundary_schemes/open_boundary_utils.jl
@@ -142,9 +142,9 @@ its own Flather profile, and the split of the inflow between the sides is left t
 carrying a `NetInflow` must carry the same one. `transport` is a number, or a `Ref` to one that may change during a
 run (from a callback, say): the pin reads it at the start of every barotropic step.
 
-The shift of each column's transport is proportional to `H^depth_exponent`, with `H` the column depth: `0` shifts the
-transport uniformly per unit length, `1` shifts the velocity uniformly (as NEMO and ROMS do), and `1/2` shifts the
-exterior free surface of the Flather condition uniformly.
+The shift of each column's transport is proportional to `H^depth_exponent`, with `H` the column depth: `0` (the default)
+shifts the transport uniformly per unit length, `1` shifts the velocity uniformly (as NEMO and ROMS do), and `1/2`
+shifts the exterior free surface of the Flather condition uniformly.
 
 ```jldoctest
 using Oceananigans
